  "body": "## Problem\nThe observer now reaches and verifies exact Vinted model filters, but VINTED_MODEL scans still pass every catalog tile through the stricter negotiation matcher. Real runtime evidence showed 96 parsed iPad 10.9 listings being reduced to `matched=0`, so `Oferty dziś` / `Oferty ten tydzień` stayed at zero even though the catalog scan itself succeeded.\n\nThe same run also showed repeated category failures on later iPad targets: the leaf category was visibly selected, but `catalog[]` sometimes did not persist within the old 5s window.\n\n## Fix\n- restore the intended split between the two observer target modes:\n  - `VINTED_MODEL`: after FilterService verifies the exact Vinted model and `brand_collection_ids[]` in the URL, count valid listing IDs from that verified catalog population directly\n  - `SEARCH_QUERY`: keep the conservative per-listing matcher and accessory filtering unchanged\n- do not loosen any real-negotiation target guards; the bypass exists only inside MarketStatsCollector\n- preserve existing price-range filtering because min/max is still applied by FilterService before the scan\n- make category persistence more tolerant: first allow normal auto-persist, then explicitly confirm the category panel if needed, and still fail closed unless `catalog[]` appears\n- add tests protecting the VINTED_MODEL vs SEARCH_QUERY counting split\n\n## Counting semantics\nBackend observation recording already refreshes `lastSeenAt` for both new and previously-known listing IDs. Calendar planning uses the observation window (`firstSeenAt < window end` and `lastSeenAt >= window start`), so re-observed known listings now correctly contribute to `Oferty dziś` and `Oferty ten tydzień` instead of remaining zero.",
